A||||2||Shawn85SE||Strut replacement?||||1||
Z||000000||Shawn85SE||06-08-2000||06:07 PM||||How hard is it to replace struts on a 85. It dosen't look hard to do. Do you have to take it to the alignment shop when your done? I got a price from the garage. $100 parts, $150 labor. Does this sound about right?<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||06-08-2000||07:57 PM||||  Shawn, you need to have, or have access to a spring compressor. You have to remove the strut/spring assembly, then press the springs off, change out the hardware, then press the spings on the new sturts. It's not hard if you know what you are doing, if not you could get in trouble. $100.00? Does that include the alignment(I hope)? I took mine off had a mechanic friend press the springs off and on (ten minutes) and replaced them myself. If you are carefull and mark the position of the struts while they are still on the vehical, you might avoid the cost of alignment, I wasn't! It cost me $45.00 for the alignment. Good luck <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000002||Uaana||06-08-2000||08:26 PM||||That sounds a little high for the hardware. I know you can get a complete set of KYB's for 189.00 US from shox.com. that's front and rear. but otherwise everything else sounds about right. as long as they include the alignment. never seen anyone able to reinstall struts without having to align them||||reg||1
